<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Revolución Libertadora</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1955–1958</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Liberating Revolution</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Revolución Libertadora, or Liberating Revolution, was the military coup of September 1955 that overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-peron">Juan Perón</a> and the military government that followed until 1958, led first by Eduardo Lonardi and then by Pedro Eugenio Aramburu. It banned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peronism">Peronism</a>, repressed a Peronist rising in 1956 with executions, and restored the constitution of 1853.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/revolucion-libertadora.jpg" alt="Revolución Libertadora" width="320" height="339" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FelipeRev · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Revoluci%C3%B3n_Libertadora_montaje.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
